From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:12:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 515/515] [DS4.1] Live-page tables: the page loop keeps its
 unrolled trip count

dgx4's first kernel bundle (2026-10-25 19:08 CET) timed decode_metadata
over each row's live pages at 1.4-1.9 us against 3.2-4.1 us at 4K-64K
contexts, and at 38 us against 1,405 us on a 16K prefill chunk, but at
6.7 us against 3.2 us at a full 1M context. The page loop had taken the
live pages' count as its bound, so it no longer unrolled, and a long
row's 32 table loads ran one after another. It keeps the table width's
trip count again, with the live pages as the predicate: a long context's
loads overlap as before, and past the live pages an iteration is a
compare.

The same run's two test fixes are already in this branch's ported tests
(the live-page commit): no step must have a live page, and the main rows
hold the step's requests in reverse and -1 past them, never a flipped
uninitialized buffer.
---
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/metadata.py | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/metadata.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/metadata.py
index 2418c2155..c8dbe8286 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/metadata.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/metadata.py
@@ -275,9 +275,12 @@ def decode_metadata_kernel(
     starts_len = T.dynamic("starts_len")
     replay_len = T.dynamic("replay_len")
     # Blocks as wide as the window part; the page part loops over the row's live
-    # pages (idle threads cost the prefill rows' blocks).
+    # pages (idle threads cost the prefill rows' blocks). The loop keeps the table
+    # width's trip count, so it unrolls and a long context's loads overlap; past the
+    # live pages an iteration is a compare.
     threads, per_thread = _threads(width)
     window_row = _window_macro(page, window, width, draft, replay, threads, per_thread)
+    main_per_thread = (main_width + threads - 1) // threads
 
     @T.prim_func
     def metadata_decode(
@@ -314,7 +317,7 @@ def decode_metadata_kernel(
                 )
                 if req < 0:
                     live = 0
-                for k in T.serial(T.ceildiv(live, threads)):
+                for k in T.serial(main_per_thread):
                     col = k * threads + tx
                     if col < live:
                         page_id = main_table[req, col]
